message: "If you use this project in your work, please cite it as below."
title: "Crowd Decoder: Mall Customer Segmentation with K-Means, Hierarchical Clustering and DBSCAN"
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Parth
    family-names: Shah
    alias: THE PARTH SHAH
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-11-21
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/ParthShah7099/Crowd_Decoder_Unsupervised_Learning"
abstract: >-
  Segments 200 mall customers into 5 groups with K-Means, Agglomerative
  Hierarchical Clustering and DBSCAN, then compares the three algorithms
  with Silhouette, Davies-Bouldin and Calinski-Harabasz scores and turns
  the segments into marketing actions.
keywords:
  - unsupervised-learning
  - clustering
  - customer-segmentation
  - k-means
  - hierarchical-clustering
  - dbscan
